From d9c9addedbd695fe7e1ec95e64131deab77933fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:49:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(redact): an error's words for a missing module are read
 before the quote, not the whole body before it (#4766)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed

missingModuleAt said a quoted name is a module an error could not load by
lowering everything before the quote. A session's body holds a place a known
value turns up at for each turn it has been in the history, and knownSpans
asks packageAt at each of them, so every such place paid the body's whole
length again — a 555 KB turn held 1m54s in the masking, past the unrouted
budget, and was answered 504 (#4766). The words stand right before the
quote; what is read of what is before them is the last 64 bytes of it now,
as assignedSecret reads the 64 before the value it judges. A letter a lower
case folds wider than in those bytes reads the whole text before the quote,
as before. Nothing of what is masked changes.

Run

- RED (product file reverted, test kept): TestMissingModuleReadsOnlyTheWordsBeforeTheQuote
  fails with "judging the words made 401440 bytes, 8 KiB at most".
- GREEN: the test passes; go test -tags nogui ./internal/redact/ passes.
- A session that grows turn by turn, Personal on and config-dense as the
  report has it: a 925 KB turn went from 3.8s to 0.76s, a 560 KB turn
  masks in 0.2s; the rest of the cost is the rules' own linear scan.
- go vet on darwin, linux/amd64 and windows/amd64; builds on all three;
  gofmt clean; BenchmarkMaskLongSession unchanged on its shape.

